IBM-ACE-On-QEMU-Reproduction, patch 0001: build parallelism

Applies to: IBM/ACE-RISCV 1ebdebf4cacc04fcb83191053b4e979cbcdcb2d6 (Apache-2.0)
Audit:      docs/SAFETY_AUDIT.md, findings A1 and A2

Why: the host is shared, and the project builds with 2 jobs (charter 4.7).
 - hypervisor/Makefile and confidential-vms/linux_vm/Makefile pass BR2_JLEVEL=0 to Buildroot,
   which means "number of CPUs + 1" jobs (21 on the reference host) and cannot be overridden.
 - hypervisor/Makefile (kvmtool) and security-monitor/Makefile (OpenSBI) write -j$(nproc).
   Inside a Makefile, $(nproc) is an undefined make variable, so the option becomes a bare -j,
   which runs an unlimited number of jobs.

What changes:
 - BR2_JLEVEL becomes a make variable with the upstream default 0 ("BR2_JLEVEL ?= 0").
 - -j$(nproc) becomes -j$(shell nproc), which is what the upstream code intends.

Behaviour without new settings: as upstream, except that -j is bounded by nproc.
This project builds with BR2_JLEVEL=2 and OMP_NUM_THREADS=2 (GNU nproc then reports 2).

